Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: Ganged IR flash LED (channels 1 and 4)

SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: Ganged IR flash LED (channels 1 and 4)

SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: Ganged IR flash LED (channels 1 and 4)

Replace the four single-channel IR discovery LEDs of 0081 by one LED node
taking PM8550 flash channels 1 and 4 together (led-sources = <1>, <4>). The
Windows driver qcpmic8380.sys drives its "LED1" as CH1 + CH4 ganged at
350 mA per channel (EMITTER-LOCATE.md, section 7), and the 12.5 mA
single-channel discovery test showed nothing on a phone camera. The
discovery LEDs are retired, not kept: two nodes owning channels 1 and 4
would share the CHAN_EN and module-enable state of the driver. The node is
named ir:flash-14.

Limits: flash-max-microamp 200000 (100 mA on each of the two channels, the
hard cap of the 0091 driver limit), flash-max-timeout-us 10000 (10 ms
hardware safety timer), color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR> so the SL7 safety lockout
(no torch, bind gate ir_test=1, 700 mA total, safety timer always on) and
the ir_max_ua limit of 0091 (default 25 mA per channel) apply. Torch is
refused in code, led-max-microamp 10000 is the binding minimum (5 mA per
channel). The node is in every DTB but binds only on the IR test boot.
No camera node refers to it.

Rationale: IR emitter bring-up, stage B.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -88,9 +88,10 @@ &cci0_i2c0 {
 	 * link to a flash LED.
 	 *
 	 * The illuminator is the PM8550 flash (QCOM0C27, 700 mA) but its
-	 * channel is unknown. The four discovery LEDs under &pm8550_flash
-	 * below are test-only and bind to nothing from this node. Do not add a
-	 * `leds = <...>` link until the channel has been found on the device
+	 * channel is probably 1 and 4 together. The ganged test LED under
+	 * &pm8550_flash below is test-only and binds to nothing from this node.
+	 * Do not add a `leds = <...>` link until the channel has been found on
+	 * the device
 	 * (see the Phase B notes). Never drive it as a continuous torch.
 	 *
 	 * The master clock is unknown: no SL7 resource file names one. MCLK0
@@ -176,18 +177,26 @@ &pcie3_phy {
  * SpiSerialBusV2 40 MHz mode 0, IRQ GPIO51, reset GPIO48, VDD enable GPIO64.
  */
 /*
- * IR illuminator DISCOVERY ONLY (SL7 local, IR emitter plan stage A/B).
+ * IR illuminator, ganged LED (SL7 local, IR emitter plan stage B).
  *
- * One LED per PM8550 flash channel, because Windows' channel is unknown. Each
- * is limited to the binding minimums: 12.5 mA flash, a 10 ms hardware safety
- * timer, and a 5 mA torch clamp (torch itself is refused in code for any LED
- * with color = IR). Replace these four nodes by one after Stage B.
+ * Windows' qcpmic8380.sys drives "LED1" as flash channels 1 and 4 together
+ * (EMITTER-LOCATE.md, section 7), so one LED node takes both: led-sources =
+ * <1 4>, the driver splits the current equally over the two channels. It
+ * replaces the four single-channel discovery LEDs, which overlapped it
+ * (channels 1 and 4 would have had two owners) and showed nothing at 12.5 mA.
+ *
+ * The device tree allows at most 100 mA per channel (flash-max-microamp
+ * 200000 for two channels, the driver's hard cap) and a 10 ms hardware safety
+ * timer (flash-max-timeout-us). The driver additionally limits the current
+ * to its ir_max_ua module parameter per channel (default 25 mA). Torch is
+ * refused in code for any LED with color = IR (led-max-microamp is only the
+ * schema minimum, 5 mA per channel). The LED is named ir:flash-14.
  *
  * The node is in the DTB of every boot entry, but it can not bind outside the
  * IR test entry: leds-qcom-flash is not loaded (modprobe gate: needs
  * sl7.ir_test=1 on the kernel command line) and, if it were loaded anyway,
  * its probe refuses IR LED nodes unless its module parameter ir_test=1
- * (set only by that gate). No camera node refers to these LEDs.
+ * (set only by that gate). No camera node refers to this LED.
  */
 &pm8550_flash {
 	status = "okay";
@@ -195,40 +204,10 @@ &pm8550_flash {
 	led-0 {
 		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
 		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
-		function-enumerator = <1>;
-		led-sources = <1>;
-		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
-		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
-		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
-	};
-
-	led-1 {
-		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
-		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
-		function-enumerator = <2>;
-		led-sources = <2>;
-		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
-		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
-		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
-	};
-
-	led-2 {
-		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
-		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
-		function-enumerator = <3>;
-		led-sources = <3>;
-		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
-		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
-		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
-	};
-
-	led-3 {
-		function = LED_FUNCTION_FLASH;
-		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_IR>;
-		function-enumerator = <4>;
-		led-sources = <4>;
-		led-max-microamp = <5000>;
-		flash-max-microamp = <12500>;
+		function-enumerator = <14>;
+		led-sources = <1>, <4>;
+		led-max-microamp = <10000>;
+		flash-max-microamp = <200000>;
 		flash-max-timeout-us = <10000>;
 	};
 };
